Subject: [PATCH] exr: buffer DWA DCT blocks one block row at a time

decode_lossy_dct_group allocated `[[f32; 64]; 3]` (768 bytes) for every 8x8
block of the chunk before decoding, also for single channels. For a 2-byte half
channel that is 6 times the pixel data, and up to 48 times for a 1 pixel wide
block, so a chunk within any sensible allocation limit (512 MiB) still asks
for gigabytes. The coefficients are consumed in block row order anyway: decode,
inverse-transform and write out one row of blocks at a time, like the C
reference does with its row block buffers.

The regression test is an integration test with a peak-counting allocator,
registered in Cargo.toml because the published manifest disables autotests.

Upstream: open PR johannesvollmer/exrs#310 (by Pixel-Minions, 2026-11-05) makes the same change (decode the lossy DCT one row of blocks at a time), pitched as a speedup; exr 1.74.3 does not have it.
Drop this patch once #310 lands in a release the image pin uses.

